  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Write a program which does the following:\n\n\nFind the area of a square of side 14 cm.\nAlso, find the cost of painting the square if the paint costs is $7 per cm2cm^2cm2.\nInitialise the following  `variables`  in your program and use them in the computation\n\n**`s`**  to store the length of side the square.\n**`area`**  to store the area of the square.\n**`cost`**  to store the cost of painting.\n\n\nOutput  **`area`**  and  **`cost`**  to the console on separate lines.",
    "constraints": [
      "Side length s = 14 cm (fixed).",
      "Paint cost per cm² = 7 dollars (fixed).",
      "Number of test cases T = 1."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "No input required.",
    "outputFormat": "First line: area of the square (in cm²). Second line: cost of painting the square (in dollars).",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "",
        "output": "196\\n1372",
        "explanation": "Area = 14 * 14 = 196 cm². Cost = 196 * 7 = 1372 dollars."
      }
    ]
  },
