  "solution": {
    "approach": "The side length of the square is given as 14 cm. Compute area = s * s. Compute cost = area * 7. Print both values on separate lines. The computation is O(1) time and O(1) memory.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\\nint main(){int T=1;for(int t=0;t<T;++t){int s=14;int area=s*s;int cost=area*7;printf(\"%d\\\\n%d\\\\n\",area,cost);}return 0;}",
      "C++": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\nusing namespace std;\\nint main(){int T=1;for(int t=0;t<T;++t){int s=14;int area=s*s;int cost=area*7;cout<<area<<'\\\\n'<<cost<<'\\\\n';}return 0;}",
      "Java": "public class Main{public static void main(String[] args){int T=1;for(int t=0;t<T;++t){int s=14;int area=s*s;int cost=area*7;System.out.println(area);System.out.println(cost);}}}",
      "Python3": "def main():\\n    T=1\\n    for _ in range(T):\\n        s=14\\n        area=s*s\\n        cost=area*7\\n        print(area)\\n        print(cost)\\nif __name__==\\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()",
      "JavaScript": "const fs=require('fs');\\nlet T=1;\\nlet out=[];\\nfor(let i=0;i<T;i++){\\n  const s=14;\\n  const area=s*s;\\n  const cost=area*7;\\n  out.push(area.toString());\\n  out.push(cost.toString());\\n}\\nconsole.log(out.join('\\\\n'));"
    },
